    files: ["k8s/cluster/cluster-secret-store.yaml"],
    body: "<p>You can see which hop failed without guessing:</p><ul><li><code>IdentityPoolDoesNotExist</code> or a metadata error: Workload Identity is off, or <code>clusterLocation</code> / <code>clusterName</code> do not match the cluster.</li><li><code>Permission 'iam.serviceAccounts.getAccessToken' denied</code>: the Kubernetes account is not a <code>workloadIdentityUser</code> on the Google account. The annotation may still look correct.</li><li><code>Permission 'secretmanager.versions.access' denied</code>: impersonation worked. The Google account is missing <code>secretAccessor</code>.</li><li><code>Secret not found</code>: impersonation worked and the role is enough. The secret name is wrong, or it is in another project. <code>projectID: surshongi</code> is the project that is searched.</li></ul><p>gcloud does not have to be installed on your Windows machine for any of this. Cloud Shell in the browser is already authenticated and already on project <code>surshongi</code>. The variable must be spelled <code>PROJECT_ID</code>. <code>PROJECt_ID</code> is a different, empty variable, and <code>gcloud config set project</code> then fails with “VALUE: Must be specified.”</p>"
